  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 35,
    "global_ayah_id": 5479,
    "tafseer": "(a) These verses give a brief description of the qualities of two types of human beings: those who will be treated as entitled to enter Paradise and those whose deeds will cause them to be thrown into Hell on Doomsday."
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 36,
    "global_ayah_id": 5480,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 37,
    "global_ayah_id": 5481,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 38,
    "global_ayah_id": 5482,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 39,
    "global_ayah_id": 5483,
    "tafseer": "(a) Those who stand by Untruth, feel that their high status is in jeopardy when the open and clear call to the Truth is delivered to them. In order to suppress this call, they try to smother it. Their unreasonable behaviour will take them straight to Hell, but with their false optimism, they go on thinking that they are fast approaching Paradise."
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 40,
    "global_ayah_id": 5484,
    "tafseer": "(b) The periodic change in the places where the sun rises and sets on the earth’s horizon is due to that unique feature of the earth known as the axial tilt. This plus the fact that the sun is at one of the foci of the earth’s elliptical orbit, and not at its centre, is responsible for the changing of the seasons. In the absence of such factors the earth would have been less useful to man."
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 41,
    "global_ayah_id": 5485,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 42,
    "global_ayah_id": 5486,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 43,
    "global_ayah_id": 5487,
    "tafseer": ""
  },
  {
    "surah_id": 70,
    "ayah_number": 44,
    "global_ayah_id": 5488,
    "tafseer": "(c) In this world when there is the example of an inferior thing being improved upon, the occurrence of similar other events is quite within the realm of the possible. Those who, in spite of such clear signs, do not learn any lessons are undoubtedly frivolous people. Such people learn lessons only when they are compelled to do so."
  }
